---
.title = "Performance",
.description = "What glowcap costs, as dated measurements you can repeat: wire-path allocation and footprint budgets the build pins, plus benchmark charts.",
.date = .date("2026-06-12T00:00:00"),
.layout = "performance.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

These charts measure glowcap's costs on one machine. Each dated snapshot
names its source and environment. [Beside other systems]($link.page('performance/compared'))
compares the same calls in Cap'n Proto RPC and Spritely Goblins.

```=html
<!-- bench:glance GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<div class="bench-glance">
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#frame-ownership-and-dispatch"><strong>1</strong><span>allocation per delivered message</span></a>
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#codec-throughput"><strong>10.6M</strong><span>messages a second through the protocol engine, without sockets</span></a>
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#per-connection-footprint"><strong>1,072 B</strong><span>of protocol state for each idle connection</span></a>
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#encrypted-transport-round-trip"><strong>58,228</strong><span>encrypted round trips a second over 16 iroh connections on one thread</span></a>
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#cost-through-each-language-binding"><strong>1 ms</strong><span>from starting the Zig client to its first finished task</span></a>
<a class="card bench-glance-card" href="#persistent-actors-in-loam"><strong>2.2 µs</strong><span>to call an actor asleep in LMDB, among 2,048</span></a>
</div>
```

```=html
<!-- bench:stamp GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<p class="bench-stamp">Benchmark snapshot of source <code>v0.1.1-72-gc49b0b78a</code> on 2026-11-05: Linux aarch64, 20 logical CPUs, 122 GiB RAM, Racket v9.3 CS, Spritely Goblins v0.18.0-52-gdcc2b2c5, and the <code>glowcap</code> archives built by Zig 0.17.0 in ReleaseFast. <code>zig build bench-site-report</code> repeats it.</p>
```

Build checks hold selected allocation, copy, and core-state size budgets.
`zig build check` fails when those budgets change. `zig build perf-check`
catches coarse timing regressions. The
[milestones to 1.0](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/milestones.md)
name the constants and tests behind the budgets.

# [Codec throughput]($section.id('codec-throughput'))

`bench-codec` encodes and decodes the same small method call with
[Syrup](https://github.com/ocapn/syrup) and Cap'n Proto. Compare nanoseconds
per message, because MB/s also reflects that Cap'n Proto emits a larger frame. The
chart shows the small call. The bench also decodes the larger
seventy-six value `report` call into borrowed views of the frame, where the Cap'n Proto
codec reads each value in place. [Codecs]($link.page('codecs')) covers the
choice.

```=html
<!-- bench:codec GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<div class="bench-panel">
<figure>
<figcaption><strong>Nanoseconds per message, lower is better.</strong></figcaption>
<div class="bench-legend"><span><i style="background:var(--teal, #257f88)"></i>Syrup</span><span><i style="background:var(--accent, #c76f18)"></i>Cap'n Proto</span></div>
