<text x="16.68%" y="15" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink, #3a3027)">115</text>
<rect x="26.18%" y="79.3" width="17.43%" height="104.7" fill="var(--accent, #c76f18)" rx="2"/>
<text x="34.9%" y="76.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink, #3a3027)">72</text>
<text x="25.79%" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft, #6b5d4d)">encode</text>
<rect x="56.38%" y="95.4" width="17.43%" height="88.6" fill="var(--teal, #257f88)" rx="2"/>
<text x="65.1%" y="92.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink, #3a3027)">61</text>
<rect x="74.61%" y="63.4" width="17.43%" height="120.6" fill="var(--accent, #c76f18)" rx="2"/>
<text x="83.32%" y="60.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill="var(--ink, #3a3027)">83</text>
<text x="74.21%" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft, #6b5d4d)">decode</text>
</svg>

</figure>
<div>
<table>
<thead><tr><th></th><th>Syrup</th><th>Cap'n Proto</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>encode ns</td><td>114.8</td><td>72.4</td></tr>
<tr><td>decode ns</td><td>61.3</td><td>83.4</td></tr>
<tr><td>encode MB/s</td><td>610</td><td>3,646</td></tr>
<tr><td>decode MB/s</td><td>1,141</td><td>3,166</td></tr>
<tr><td>frame bytes</td><td>70</td><td>264</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
</div>
<p class="bench-note">The protocol engine alone, with no sockets, handles 10,573,127 inbound messages a second, and adds an entry to a sparse import table in 44.6 ns.</p>
```

# [Per-connection footprint]($section.id('per-connection-footprint'))

`bench-peer-scaling` counts inline and heap memory in each state: idle
(accepted, awaiting its first message), warmed (one export and one delivered message),
sixteen live exports, and served with a vat. The half-million column
is arithmetic over core memory, not RSS or a live network test.

