# [Persistent actors in Loam]($section.id('persistent-actors-in-loam'))

[Loam]($link.page('loam')) keeps actors in a database and loads one only when a
call reaches it. `bench-loam` builds a graph of conversations in LMDB (a memory-mapped key-value database) and grows
it from 64 to 2,048. A call to an asleep actor pays one record load. Each
conversation costs a small, fixed amount of Zig heap, far less than its records
on disk. A restart loads only the record its first call needs. The
[workload notes](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/bench/loam/README.md)
describe each phase.

